  "generated_text": "Given that \\(\\gcd(a,b) = 168\\) and \\(\\gcd(a,c) = 693\\), we need to find the smallest possible value of \\(\\gcd(b,c)\\).\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of 168 and 693:\n\\[\n168 = 2^3 \\times 3 \\times 7\n\\]\n\\[\n693 = 3 \\times 7 \\times 11\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\gcd(a,b) = 168\\) and \\(\\gcd(a,c) = 693\\), \\(a\\) must be a common factor of both 168 and 693. Therefore, \\(a\\) must include the least \n3\n\n\n    3, 7, and 11 in its prime factorization.\n\n\n, thegcdgcd  )        3  3  3  3  3  3                3  3  3  3  3      1}",
